# net-handlers.allowlist — baseline for the net-handler guard gate (tools/check-net-handlers.sh)
#
# Every raw net.Receive("LITERAL") site in windswept/ + windswept-colony/ (excluding thirdparty)
# must have its netstring listed here, or the gate fails. This is a RATCHET: new client->server
# handlers must go through ws.action.Register (the SWEP analogue is ws.weapon.NetReceive) — those
# wrappers use a variable netstring, so they never appear as net.Receive("LITERAL") and never need
# listing. A raw net.Receive only belongs here when it genuinely can't use a primitive:
#   - server->client RECEIVERS (the trusted direction; the bulk of this list) — cl_* sync/notify/UI-open
#   - pre-character (no character yet, so ws.access checks don't apply): wsCharacterChoose/Create/Delete
#   - the slot-coordinate move: wsInventoryMove
#   - player-field sessions (authorize via client.wsX, not ent:GetUser()): wsShipmentUse/Close, wsVendor* (C->S)
#   - two-phase approval-token auth (not active-weapon): wsCameraPhotoData
#   - intrinsic-guard SWEP with no payload: wsZipTieUse
# Other pre-existing C->S handlers here (document/container/knockout/storage/wallet/currency/radio-voice/
# recognize/suicide/signature/bag) predate this gate; migrating them is future work, not a regression.
#
# To add a handler: prefer ws.action.Register. If a raw net.Receive is genuinely correct, add its
# netstring below (keep sorted) so the addition is a conscious, reviewable line in the diff.
# Generated baseline: 2026-06-21. One netstring per line; '#' comments and blank lines ignored.

